-<section class="methodology-section" id="methodology" aria-labelledby="method-title"><div class="section-wrap two-column"><div><p class="eyebrow">Open numbers. No magic.</p><h2 id="method-title">Useful data.<br>Honest limits.</h2><p class="method-lede">This is an independent statistics project, not a system for finding winning tickets. Every ticket is independent. The house edge remains.</p><a class="text-link" href="/about">Full sources & methodology ↗</a><div class="source-card"><strong>Data you can inspect</strong><p>Florida Lottery game API, prize tiers and public winner reports. Updated automatically; suspect records are excluded from recommendations.</p><a href="/data.json" download>Download the full snapshot ↗</a></div></div><div class="faq-list"><details open><summary>What does “estimated payout” mean?</summary><p>Expected payout per dollar across a modeled remaining ticket pool. Unsold ticket counts are not public. We estimate inventory from the fraction of prizes unclaimed; this assumption can be wrong. A ticket returning less than $1 per $1 has a modeled loss.</p></details><details><summary>Are these the current odds of winning?</summary><p>Overall and profit odds come from the published prize structure. Estimated remaining-ticket payouts use unclaimed prize data, which can include already sold tickets awaiting a claim. They are different measurements and should not be treated as guaranteed current odds.</p></details><details><summary>Why do two tickets with the same name differ?</summary><p>Different game numbers identify different releases. Always match the game number on your ticket. Each release has its own prize counts, published odds and deadlines.</p></details><details><summary>Does a winning retailer improve my chances?</summary><p>Historical winner locations reflect sales volume and reporting, not a store being due for a win. We do not know a retailer’s current ticket inventory and do not recommend stores based on past winners.</p></details><details><summary>What happens when the data looks wrong?</summary><p>We reconcile advertised prize tiers with counts, label source limitations and exclude invalid odds records from recommendation lists. Source updates can lag. Always check the official game page before buying.</p></details><details><summary>How is this site funded?</summary><p>Optional Ko-fi support and clearly labeled sponsorships. Sponsors cannot buy a higher ticket ranking or change the calculations. Core comparisons are free. Cloudflare provides aggregate traffic and performance analytics.</p></details></div></div></section>
